  "description": "Fixed passive queries, fixed macOS installation-location Finder requests and explicit original-owned read-only installation checks; explicitly confirmed installed-helper preparation and normal Quit, not Installer changes; finite local configuration, workflows, public metadata and saved-version edits; explicitly confirmed nonpublishing Store access checks using assigned local credentials, separately authorized local release-history and Store preparation/execution/reconciliation through original native owners, reviewed saved offline checks, Android builds, unsigned full-Xcode Mac archives and owned build-input recovery; qualified session or encrypted credential management. Store mutations still require project opt-in, reviewed original intent, assigned credentials and one-use confirmation; this capability grants no general Store or network authority. GitHub preflight permits only publisher-bound caller review, one-use nonpublishing dispatch and exact original-run observation. Build-tool preparation permits only separately admitted fixed public-source staging with one-use Start, not arbitrary download URLs or automatic installation. Build tools can execute trusted project code only under native runtime/tool custody. GitHub repository settings permit only separately reviewed, one-use Actions-enabled or workflow-token-policy changes on the same connected registered project. Setup publication permits only separately reviewed saved configuration plus four canonical callers on a new branch and draft PR, and read-only reconciliation of original durable intents. Agent-requested project identity changes retain their separate explicit grant and review. Android upload-key setup permits only separately qualified, explicitly confirmed generation for a new application into encrypted storage; no implicit replacement of an existing key. Shared version counter connection permits only explicit selected-account fixed-counter reads and a reviewed local private-state enrollment; it never creates a counter, allocates a version or establishes Store readiness. Repository creation permits only a separately reviewed empty repository on the verified account or explicitly selected organization, private by default, with a durable one-attempt fence and GET-only reconciliation; it does not initialize, commit or push local files. No general HTTP, arbitrary remote writes, event emission, filesystem, shell or opener authority; listen/unlisten is for owner status only.",
